A||||4||Homicidal||What does the factory sub sound like???||||5||
Z||000000||Homicidal||05-01-2000||09:23 PM||||How much bass does it add?  Does it compliment the system nicely?  Is it worth trying to find one if I already have a 10" sub?||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||05-02-2000||07:45 AM||||1. Not very impressive<BR>2. Very little<BR>3. I'm sure it was bomb in 1985, but so was Kajagoogoo.<BR>4. No||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||05-02-2000||01:36 PM||||If the subwoofer and speakers aren't blown and you like to hear music, it sounds ok.<P>If you want to drive around in a boom box and let everyone else in a 500 foot radius listen to your musical tastes, the stock system will not impress you, but you'll be able to hear again when the car is turned off.<BR>******<BR>They have a noise ordinence up here and the sound police check out the muzack from your car.  If it registers on their meter at 50 feet, $100 fine plus the car is impounded, so another $50 to get it from the impound.<P>There is a ricer in my neighbor hood I can hear when he turn onto the street, and I'm inside my house.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 05-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Homicidal||05-02-2000||04:05 PM||||I'm in between.  I LOVE to listen to music, but I ALSO like to feel it.<P>I don't care if people around me can, I just care about IN the car.  My 10" compliments all my music nicely, from rap to rock to techno.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||05-02-2000||06:59 PM||||It works pretty well to provide the bottom end. If you are looking for the unnatural pounding bass, it won't do it. It will burst into flames and torch the car.<P>Since I like bottom end, but I'm not trying to hear the ending note of Lucky Man at 100 dB, I'm quite satisfied. It comes *close* to sounding like a nice pair of 6x9's in a large trunk.<P>I would call it "nice" but nothing more. ||||reg||1
